{
 "description": "Retrieval tuning grid for search_knowledge (G2-2 review). Real multilingual-e5-small, fault catalog (31 faults) + vehicle-defs docs/ideas. No ride data.",
 "method": [
  "Parameters: min_similarity (vector cosine floor, E5_MIN_COSINE) and lexical_top_n (a group with no vector evidence survives only if it is within the first N BM25 groups; 0 = vector only). The old relative cutoff on fused RRF scores was removed: RRF scores are rank-based, so 0.55 x best silently meant 'must be in both lists' and killed vector-only (cross-lingual) hits.",
  "Chosen on the tune split only: highest mean tune MRR, ties within 0.005 broken by fewer weak-query hits and then the smaller lexical_top_n.",
  "The holdout split (62 catalog complaint phrases per locale, not written by the tuner) was a veto only: no setting that loses more than 0.05 absolute holdout recall@5 against the no-floor setting was accepted. This vetoed floors above 0.83, which the tune split alone preferred (0.85 to 0.88).",
  "Holdout index: built with --exclude-holdout, i.e. the held-out phrases are removed from their complaint chunks and from the fault chunk 'Complaints:' line, so each query is a phrase the index has never seen (with the phrases indexed the holdout saturates at 1.0 and measures nothing).",
  "Baseline: hybrid RRF without the G2-2 changes (no Turkish stems, no synonyms, no stopword dropping, no floor, no lexical gate).",
  "Caveat: the eval index was assembled from the live catalog rows of an earlier local index (the live server was not reachable with the available token) and a fresh chunking of vehicle-defs/docs/ideas; faults/complaints are identical to the live catalog of 2026-11-26."
 ],
